# http-plain — notes

Phase 1 device adapter: a conservative plain HTTP/1.0-ish listener.

## What devices can send

- `GET`, `HEAD`, `POST` only (anything else → 405).
- `HTTP/1.0` and `HTTP/1.1` request lines; extra spaces tolerated; the response
  status line mirrors the request version.
- Request targets:
  - proxy-style absolute form: `GET https://host/path?q HTTP/1.1`
  - gateway path-prefix form: `GET /https://host/path?q HTTP/1.0`
  - `//host/path` (scheme-relative) treated as `http://host/path`
  - absolute form aimed at the gateway itself is unwrapped when the path
    carries a scheme prefix (proxy-style devices following a rewritten
    `Location`).
- Bodies via `Content-Length` only; `Transfer-Encoding` is rejected (400).
- Obs-fold (continuation lines) tolerated, bounded by total header limits.
- Percent-encoding is decoded strictly: malformed sequences are rejected (400),
  never guessed.

## Limits (listener hard caps, config-driven)

| Limit | Default | Failure |
| --- | --- | --- |
| request line bytes | 2048 | 431 |
| header line bytes | 2048 | 431 |
| header count | 64 | 431 |
| total header bytes | 8192 | 431 |
| body bytes | 65536 | 413 |

Profile limits (e.g. `generic-constrained` header budget of 2048) are enforced
on top at IR construction time.

## Responses

- `Connection: close` always; no chunked responses; `Content-Length` always
  emitted (except 204).
- Only the PROTOCOL §6 allowlist is emitted; header values are scrubbed of
  CR/LF/NUL (response-splitting defence).
- Errors are tiny ASCII bodies: `Code: text` + `trace: <id>` — no paths, no
  stack traces, no internal hostnames.

## Quirks still unverified

Real-device fixtures (Pocket IE, S60, PSP quirks) are Phase 2/3 work; probe
rules here are intentionally generic (`MIDP`/`J2ME` UA → `j2me-midp2-generic`,
otherwise `generic-constrained`).
